{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 53, :comments ["Each one said, 'May the Elohim of our fathers judge between us.' Jacob meant the Elohim of Abraham, while Laban meant the Elohim of Nahor his grandfather, who was an idol worshipper — and so Joshua testified." "<b>And Jacob swore by the Fear of his father.</b> By the one whom his father feared. Some say this 'Fear' alludes to the day of the Binding [of Isaac], and it is not far-fetched."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:42.905010325Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}